\n" [:p {} "In her absence the best known vaulter was American " [:a {:href "/athletes/114797"} "Jenn Suhr"] ", the defending gold medallist and the 2016 World Indoor Champion, but after qualifying, Suhr became quite ill in Rio and wasn’t sure if she could even compete in the final. After the 4.80 height, the leader was New Zealander " [:a {:href "/athletes/131264"} "Eliza McCartney"] ", who was clear, as five vaulters remained. Suhr had gone out at 4.70. At 4.85, only Greece’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/124669"} "Ekaterini Stefanidi"] " and American " [:a {:href "/athletes/132047"} "Sandi Morris"] " were successful, both on their second attempt, giving McCartney the bronze medal. Neither Stefanidi nor Morris could clear 4.90, and the Greek won the gold medal because of fewer misses, Morris having one early miss at 4.70."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "805"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/124669"} "Aikaterini Stefanidi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GRE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GRE.png"}] "GRE"]] [:td {} "4.60 (1)"] [:td {} "4.85 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1360"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/132047"} "Sandi Morris"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "4.55 (=8)"] [:td {} "4.85 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1076"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/131264"} "Eliza McCartney"]] [:td {} [:a {:h